KG42.register("source_edge_archive-f9ad9639259d5fa772a5f343",{"id":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v141-c-R007::E::v141-c-R007-E001","paper":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","rule_ref":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v141-c-R007","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R007-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e004"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-fc19e7c39ea9de54","target":"COMP-a607cc256fbfc1eb","source_occurrence_id":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v141-c-R007::V::coordination.local_operator","target_occurrence_id":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v141-c-R007::V::settlement.payment","source_unit_id":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","target_unit_id":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Consumer electricity bills under P2P sharing compared with P2G trading. | Customer billing in the proposed two-stage P2P sharing arrangement. | Electricity-bill payments and repayments of prosumers and consumers contracted with the ESC. | Individual customer settlement in the ESC-operated P2P sharing community. | Individual prosumer and consumer financial outcomes under modified SDR pricing compared with conventional P2G trading. | Prosumer electricity-bill values in the reported financial assessment. | The reported sensitivity evaluation across the studied penetration levels of PV battery systems. | The source’s explanation of prosumer income and consumer benefits under uncompensated SDR pricing.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e004","v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e013","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g04-E10","v141-b-g04-E13","v141-b-g04-E15","v141-b-g04-E17"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"fbac4b14dc3a60ce018abc1ddf626a46537061e7f5f24cbe0daf79dc35417f72","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"The ESC is responsible for exporting power to or importing power from the main grid to ensure the community's power balance. Scope: ESC responsibility at the community's interface with the main grid in the P2P sharing mechanism. The ESC is responsible for controlling the charging and discharging activities of all batteries and provides control signals to the battery controllers through one-way communication. Scope: ESC-operated aggregated battery control in the P2P sharing community. Under this shared-responsibility rule, the ESC provides each individual battery controller with the same control signal. Scope: The adopted shared-responsibility rule for community battery control. Condition: Battery charging/discharging power normalized to each battery's nominal capacity is assumed to be the same.","target_definition":"The ESC administers settlement by calculating individual customer energy bills and ensuring that prosumers’ income balances consumers’ expenditure. Scope: Individual customer settlement in the ESC-operated P2P sharing community. Local P2P pricing determines the electricity bills that prosumers pay or receive as repayments and that consumers pay. Scope: Electricity-bill payments and repayments of prosumers and consumers contracted with the ESC. The source states that the P2P buying-price ceiling implies lower consumer electricity bills under P2P sharing than under P2G trading. Scope: Consumer electricity bills under P2P sharing compared with P2G trading. Condition: The P2P buying price never exceeds the price of electricity bought from the grid. Under this uncompensated pricing case, the source states that prosumer income is undermined while consumers benefit; prosumers may receive less income than without P2P sharing. Scope: The source’s explanation of prosumer income and consumer benefits under uncompensated SDR pricing. Condition: The compensating price is zero and the supply-to-demand ratio exceeds one, so both P2P prices equal the grid selling price. At every studied penetration level, zero compensation is reported to leave some prosumers paying higher electricity bills or receiving lower incomes when participating in P2P sharing. Scope: The reported sensitivity evaluation across the studied penetration levels of PV battery systems. Condition: The compensating price is zero in the reported evaluation. With an appropriate compensating price, modified local SDR pricing is stated to ensure economic benefits for every individual prosumer and consumer, with economic gains described in terms of bill savings or repayments. Scope: Individual prosumer and consumer financial outcomes under modified SDR pricing compared with conventional P2G trading. Condition: The compensating price is appropriately set. Billing is conducted 24 hours after actual electricity consumption using recorded import/export energy data from smart meters, for example half-hourly records. Scope: Customer billing in the proposed two-stage P2P sharing arrangement. The positive value is the amount of electricity bill the prosumer is required to pay. Scope: Prosumer electricity-bill values in the reported financial assessment. Condition: The reported prosumer bill value is positive. The negative value denotes income received by the prosumer. Scope: Prosumer electricity-bill values in the reported financial assessment. Condition: The reported prosumer bill value is negative.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The ESC administers settlement by calculating individual customer energy bills and ensuring that prosumers’ income balances consumers’ expenditure. Scope: Individual customer settlement in the ESC-operated P2P sharing community.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e004"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e002","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":"264","section":"2.1. P2P energy sharing structure","anchor_text":"surplus PV power from prosumers can also be traded with consumers who do not have PV systems. PP A t","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A third party entity named “energy sharing coordinator (ESC)” coordinates between customers and provides P2P sharing services, i.e. assuring the power balance and payment balance [13]. The ESC is the controller of the DERs as well as the local market operator. The ESC is located at the PCC (e.g. the low voltage substation). A smart meter is installed at the PCC, measuring the real-time net power consumption of the community, and this measurement is the input of the ESC. The ESC is communicated with the controllers of these small-scale batteries at the prosumer premises, and provides control signals to them via one-way communication. Through managing the battery charging/discharging, the ESC ensures the maximum use of local energy resources and the minimum amount of electricity fed back into the grid. Therefore the overall energy cost of the community is reduced, and the reduced cost is distributed to individual customers through a P2P pricing mechanism. The ESC also calculates energy bills of individual customers based on the P2P pricing mechanism, using the recorded import/export energy (e.g. half-hourly) from smart meters at the premises."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e004","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":"264","section":"2.1. P2P energy sharing structure","anchor_text":"Details of the control framework and the pricing mechanism for the local market are presented in Sec","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"(1) Energy sharing coordinator (ESC)\n• Export power to (or import power from) the main grid to ensure the power balance of the community;\n• Contract with a supplier for the electricity trade at pre-defined exporting/importing prices and ensure the payment balance between the community and the supplier;\n• Control the charging/discharging activities of all batteries;\n• Contract with individual prosumers and consumers according to the P2P pricing mechanism and ensure the prosumers’ income balance with the consumers’ expenditure."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Consumer electricity bills under P2P sharing compared with P2G trading. | Customer billing in the proposed two-stage P2P sharing arrangement. | Electricity-bill payments and repayments of prosumers and consumers contracted with the ESC. | Individual customer settlement in the ESC-operated P2P sharing community. | Individual prosumer and consumer financial outcomes under modified SDR pricing compared with conventional P2G trading. | Prosumer electricity-bill values in the reported financial assessment. | The reported sensitivity evaluation across the studied penetration levels of PV battery systems. | The source’s explanation of prosumer income and consumer benefits under uncompensated SDR pricing.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e004","v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e013","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g04-E10","v141-b-g04-E13","v141-b-g04-E15","v141-b-g04-E17"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R007-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e004"]},"paper_scope_note":"Electricity bill settlement directly depends on the post-metering price; the revenue improvement is a conditional statement and sensitivity case in the paper, not a general proposition independently verified in this work."}});
